  "notes": "{満|み}ちる means to become full or reach capacity, often used for natural phenomena.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive)\n- Pair: {満|み}たす (transitive, to fill)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {月|つき}が{満|み}ちる: the moon becomes full\n- {潮|しお}が{満|み}ちる: the tide comes in\n- {心|こころ}が{喜|よろこ}びで{満|み}ちる: to be filled with joy\n- {期間|きかん}が{満|み}ちる: a period expires\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {満月|まんげつ}: full moon\n- {満潮|みちしお}/{満|み}ち{潮|しお}: high tide\n- {満|み}ち{足|た}りる: to be satisfied\n\nCONTRAST:\n- {欠|か}ける: to wane, be lacking",
